    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.75) anchoring the offense as our clear top play. Facing a favorable matchup against Liberatore (xERA 4.28), **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a strong park factor and a premium spot in the two-hole, making him the highest-ceiling asset in the lineup. Close behind, **Gunnar Henderson** (67.13) warrants a strong start despite a difficult matchup against Wheeler. While Wheeler\u2019s elite arm usually suppresses output, the combination of a high park factor and **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s dynamic platoon advantage keeps his efficiency score well within the recommended range. We are also tracking **Andy Pages** (62.47) and **Jackson Merrill** (63.54) as high-leverage plays; **Andy Pages** benefits specifically from an opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which enhances his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor given our strategic emphasis on speed.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Wade Meckler** (35.18), who sat on the bubble of our 40-point efficiency floor. While **Wade Meckler**\u2019s platoon edge and high recency metrics were enticing, the brutal matchup against Misiorowski (xERA 2.07) ultimately cratered his projection, forcing him to the bench. We are playing it safe by avoiding such a significant SP skill penalty. Meanwhile, caution is advised regarding **Liam Hicks** (57.75) and **Drake Baldwin** (51.18); although both carry solid efficiency scores, their reliance on favorable platoon splits against Stock and Cavalli leaves them susceptible to volatility. We are currently monitoring **Jordan Westburg**\u2019s ongoing IL status, which remains a significant void in our infield depth, and we will continue to rotate peripheral options like **Denzer Guzman** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to preserve our game caps until a more favorable entry point arises.",
